    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/05027ACF42B26FF3DD70CE4664A18E9F/jobs/586755": {
      "title": "Leadership - Adjunct",
      "description": "Leadership - Adjunct You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Leadership - Adjunct Edmond, OK 73034 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Category OTRS Ineligible Apply Description Note: Adjunct positions at UCO are part-time teaching positions. This posting is to create a pool of interested applicants from which the Department may draw as sections become open at any point in the current academic year. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of adjuncts. Adjunct faculty members provide quality learning experience for students and support the educational philosophy, mission, and long-term goals of the University of Central Oklahoma, the College of Liberal Arts, and the hiring department. Adjunct faculty members teach classes, advise and mentor students, evaluate student performance, and maintain student records in accordance with university policies. Adjunct faculty members work in a collaborative manner with full- and part-time colleagues and adhere to all of the policies and procedures outlined in the UCO Faculty and Employee Handbooks. Overview: The College of Liberal Arts seeks qualified instructors interested in teaching 1, 2, and 3 credit hour courses on leadership. Courses include topics such as leadership theories, leadership in ethics, business ethics, ethics in public service, group dynamics, leadership communication and many others. Instructors are responsible for course delivery, grading, and facilitating student engagement in on-campus classes. Job Duties: Deliver engaging, high-quality instruction in alignment with approved syllabus objectives and curriculum. Foster an interactive learning environment through classroom discussions, case studies, and practical exercises. Evaluate student assignments, exams, and projects, providing constructive and timely feedback. Maintain regular communication with students. Adhere to university academic policies, grading deadlines, and administrative procedures. Required Qualifications: Education: Master’s degree in Leadership, Organizational Development, Communication, Management, Public Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Experience: 2+ years of professional leadership, management, or executive experience in corporate, non-profit, or governmental sectors. Preferred Qualifications: Prior teaching experience at the college or university level. Physical Demands: Reasonable accommodations (in accordance with ADA requirements) may be made, upon request, to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Application Requirements: Cover letter should include: Which Leadership (LEAD prefix) courses at UCO you are qualified and interested in teaching. Information on your availability to teach (i.e. daytime classes, evenings, and/or weekends). Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
