      "title": "Information Systems and Operations Management, Adjunct",
      "description": "Information Systems and Operations Management, Adjunct You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Information Systems and Operations Management, Adjunct Edmond, OK 73034 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Category OTRS Ineligible Apply Description Position Overview: Note: Adjunct positions at UCO are part-time teaching positions. This posting is to create a pool of interested applicants from which the Department may draw as sections become open at any point in the current academic year. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of adjuncts. Adjunct Faculty provides a quality learning experience for students on a semester basis. Adjunct faculty reports to a dean or chair and performs instruction-related duties and responsibilities in a timely manner and in accordance with the mission, policies, and procedures of the college. The relationship of the adjunct faculty member to the student is one of teacher and facilitator of learning. Department Specific Essential Job Functions: University of Central Oklahoma, Dept. of Information Systems & Operations Management, invites applications for adjunct positions to teach information systems courses, operations management courses, or supply chain management courses. A master's degree in Information Systems, Operations, or Supply Chain related field. MBA degrees are considered with undergraduate degrees or work experience in information systems, operations management, or supply chain management. Experience in the one of the above industries related to the teaching area is required. This posting is to create a pool of interested applicants from which the Department may draw as sections become open at any point in the current academic year. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of adjuncts. Both day, evening, and online courses are offered by the department. Experience Required: Possesses at least a master's degree in the field specified in the position announcement (exceptions require Academic Affairs approval). Possesses excellent communication, problem-solving, and organizational skills. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Master's degree in information systems, operations management, or supply chain management preferred. MBA with experience in information systems, operations management, or supply chain management is also appropriate. No engineering degrees will be considered for these business classes. Physical Demands: Reasonable accommodations (in accordance with ADA requirements) may be made, upon request, to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
